text:
sam: heads-up — triaging a small but annoying doc drift: error-ref/timeouts.md still suggests using client-side retries for streaming requests. that's led to a few user reports where retrying a stream caused duplicated tokens. need a short PR to clarify streaming vs non-streaming retry guidance and add a small example showing safe retry boundary.

ana: omg yes. saw a support ticket where a customer retried the whole stream and got duplicate paragraphs. we should recommend idempotent checkpoints and using the SDK's resume token when possible.

li: i can draft the snippet. propose adding a tiny example: show using `sdk.stream.resume()` with an idempotency key instead of naive fetch retry. also call out 429 vs 504 semantics.

kevin: also add a one-line caveat on context-window trimming: trimming the oldest user message can shift the model behavior. recommend trimming assistant tokens first, then user, then system as last resort.

sam: good. pls also make sure timeout examples include both short client timeouts (e.g., 30s) and server-side SLO guidance. we should surface the recommended fallback order: (1) quick retry with jitter, (2) fallback to smaller model variant if latency persists, (3) degrade gracefully to cached response.

ana: suggest we include a mini table for backoff parameters (attempts, base-delay, max-delay, jitter). short and actionable.

li: snippet draft:```js
// safe streaming retry (pseudocode)
const key = makeIdempotencyKey(req);
const stream = await sdk.stream.create({ model: 'gpt-mini', idempotencyKey: key });
try {
  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    process(chunk);
  }
} catch (e) {
  if (isTransient(e) && stream.resumeToken) {
    // resume from token instead of restarting whole prompt
    const resumed = await sdk.stream.resume(stream.resumeToken, { idempotencyKey: key });
  } else {
    // fallback flow
  }
}
```

kevin: nice. add inline note: // resumeToken may not be available for some legacy models — fall back to checkpointing on client side.

docs-bot: lint-check triggered for PR draft — markdown-lint: warn long-line in the backoff table; linkcheck: one internal link 404 -> error-ref/streaming.md; spellcheck: 0 warnings.

sam: thanks. li, can you open a draft PR and tag me + ana? please include a short migration snippet for teams still using old retry header patterns.

li: opened draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1102 — includes snippet, backoff table, and a short paragraph about prompt-trimming ordering. tagged sam/ana for review.

ana: reviewing now. left minor phrasing suggestions and added a note to link StreamInterrupts -> streaming.md. also replaced an external blog link with our archived internal runbook copy.

kevin: i pushed a small addition to the backoff table: recommended max attempts = 5 for streaming, 3 for non-streaming.

docs-bot: docs-ci: 3/3 checks passed. preview deploy available at https://docs-preview.redwood/error-ref/timeouts?pr=1102.

sam: looks good. merging after a short smoke test. once merged, can we add an entry to docs changelog and a short blurb in #release-notes?

li: merged and updated CHANGELOG.md (docs v1.15.0). posting summary in #release-notes now. :rocket:

ana: thanks all. follow-up: let's add a unit test in docs-examples repo that runs the streaming snippet in a sandbox to prevent regressions. opened follow-up issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs-examples/issues/78

sam: great catch everyone — closing thread after release-note verification.
